  "notes": "Cash-basis village (FYE 9/30/2025). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); business-type lines from the Total Proprietary Funds column (p7): Sewer, Water, Solid Waste. Governmental roll-forward: 428,559 + 398,146 - 432,795 + 28,830 - 28,830 = 393,910 (fund balances). business_type roll-forward: 295,433 + 283,676 - 306,016 = 273,093; debt payments, interest expense and capital outlay are nonoperating disbursements on p7 so recorded as disbursements. Business-type totals are computed (statement prints operating and nonoperating subtotals only). Balance sheet uses the Total column of the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1); no liabilities shown. The only supplementary schedule is one combined budget schedule for governmental and proprietary funds (p8) with a single Original/Final budget column; its Taxes line (118,560) is split into property and sales tax using the p3/p5 amounts; 'Intergovernmental' (88,721) does not tie to the fund statements (p5) and is recorded as printed; 'Local' (474,541, budget 567,812) is recorded as one printed line on the combined schedule (not split by fund type, since the page does not itemize it). Transfers in 28,830 appear inside the schedule's Total Receipts and transfers out inside Total Disbursements (marked includes other financing). All lines of the combined budget schedule carry fund 'All funds (governmental and proprietary)' so they tie to its printed totals; the Sewer/Water/Solid Waste lines are business-type with the fund name in department. Read pages 1-8 of 8."
